      "points": [
        "The correlation of 0.641 means tracts ranking higher in violations per 1,000 adults also rank higher in high blood pressure prevalence",
        "Census Tract 12 had the highest violations per 1,000 adults at 645.4 and the highest high blood pressure rate at 59.2%",
        "Census Tract 11 ranked second in violations per 1,000 adults at 608.4 and second in high blood pressure at 60.1%",
        "Census Tract 22.02 ranked third in violations per 1,000 adults at 536.2 and third in high blood pressure at 57.8%",
        "The pattern holds across the full list: higher violations per 1,000 adults correspond with higher high blood pressure rates in every row"
      ],
      "caveats": [
        "CDC high blood pressure figures are model-based estimates from survey data, not direct measurements",
        "2026 code violation data is partial (through October 2026) and may not represent the full year",
        "All tracts in the result set share the exact same correlation value (0.641), so ranking strength depends on the underlying variable distributions rather than variation in the correlation itself"
